<Project>

  <!--
    Q8.11 — the third-party half of "stop the CS8002 warnings".

    Every first-party assembly is now strong-named, so the only remaining CS8002 sources are unsigned *third-party*
    references, which are not ours to sign. The one live case is Scriban (the benchmark comparison engine), referenced
    by the signed src/Heddle.Performance.

    Roslyn has no per-reference suppression for CS8002 — the warning carries no source location and the Csc task reads
    only a project-wide disabled-warning list; NoWarn metadata on a PackageReference is a NuGet (NU*) mechanism and was
    measured to have no effect on CS8002. So the narrowest suppression the compiler actually supports is applied here,
    and it is narrowed two further ways rather than being a blanket project setting:

      * it is keyed on the *named* third-party assembly below, so it applies only in projects that really reference it,
        and nowhere else in the repository; and
      * it applies only to signed projects, because CS8002 cannot arise in an unsigned one.

    An unsigned reference that is NOT on this list therefore still warns wherever it appears — which is the point: the
    list is a declaration of which third-party assemblies we have accepted unsigned, reviewable as a list. Residual,
    stated rather than hidden: a project that referenced both a listed and an unlisted unsigned assembly would have
    both warnings suppressed together, because the compiler cannot distinguish them. No project does today.

    Stated here rather than in the referencing project because src/Heddle.Performance is under an explicit
    change-nothing ruling (Q7.2 — a benchmark effort is mid-flight there).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <HeddleAcceptedUnsignedReference Include="Scriban" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="HeddleAcceptUnsignedThirdPartyReferences"
          BeforeTargets="CoreCompile"
          Condition="'$(SignAssembly)' == 'true' and '@(HeddleAcceptedUnsignedReference)' != ''">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_HeddleAcceptedUnsignedHit Include="@(ReferencePathWithRefAssemblies)"
                                  Condition="'%(Filename)' == 'Scriban'" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <PropertyGroup Condition="'@(_HeddleAcceptedUnsignedHit)' != ''">
      <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS8002</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
